# The Mycosynth Gardens' "{X}, {T}: This land becomes a copy of target nontoken artifact you control with mana value X."
# With X = 1 and exactly {1} paid (Mox Jet's B, the pool checked empty right after), the only legal targets are Bot1's
# nontoken artifacts of mana value 1: Sol Ring. Refused, each for its one reason: Bot1's Mox Jet (mana value 0) and Gold Pan
# (mana value 2) are the wrong value, Bot1's Treasure token is a token, and Bot2's Sol Ring (mana value 1) is not
# controlled by Bot1. The Gardens becomes a Sol Ring (CR 707.2) that stays tapped from the cost, beside the untapped
# original (the first Sol Ring is the Gardens, on the battlefield first): no longer a land, so it is an Artifact with no
# Land type.

[Bot1 Deck]
The Mycosynth Gardens
Mox Jet
Sol Ring
Gold Pan
Island x3
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Sol Ring
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.The Mycosynth Gardens.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.The Mycosynth Gardens.Activate(Ability: Add {C})
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Gold Pan.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.The Mycosynth Gardens.Activate(Ability: becomes; X: 1)
! Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet; Gold Pan; Treasure Token; Bot2.Battlefield.Sol Ring)
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring)
Bot1.Choose(Close mana window)
Bot1.Choose(Pay mana)
? Bot1.Mana = 
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Gold Pan; Mox Jet; Sol Ring; Sol Ring; Treasure Token
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring#1.Types = Artifact
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring#2.Types = Artifact
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring#1.Subtypes = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring#1.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring#2.Tapped = false
Bot1.Battlefield.Treasure Token.Token = true
Stack.Count = 0
